# 5. AUTHENTICATION AND ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT

Implement a complete authentication workflow.

## 5.1 Registration

Create a registration page with:

- Full name.
- Email address.
- Password.
- Confirm password.
- Terms acceptance where appropriate.

Validation requirements:

1. Email addresses must be valid and normalized.
2. Each normalized email address can belong to only one account.
3. Passwords must contain more than eight characters, meaning at least nine characters.
4. Passwords must contain at least one uppercase letter.
5. Passwords must contain at least one lowercase letter.
6. Passwords must contain at least one special character.
7. Passwords must be stored only as secure password hashes.
8. Duplicate registration attempts must return useful validation errors.
9. Customer registration must never allow the user to select an administrator or staff role.

Create new public registrations with the `CUSTOMER` role.

## 5.2 Login

Provide:

- Email and password authentication.
- Password visibility toggle.
- Form validation.
- Invalid-credentials feedback.
- Loading indicators.
- Secure session handling.
- Logout functionality.
- Protected routes.
- Role-aware navigation.

## 5.3 Password reset

Implement:

1. A forgot-password page.
2. Email submission.
3. Secure, cryptographically random, single-use reset tokens.
4. Expiration of reset tokens.
5. Email delivery of the reset link when email configuration is available.
6. Password reset confirmation.
7. Invalidation of the token after use.
8. Appropriate invalidation of existing sessions when required.

Avoid revealing whether an email address is registered.

If SMTP is not configured, provide a development-only email preview or a clearly documented local testing mechanism. Never claim an email was delivered when it was not.

