`Draft → Quotation → Confirmed → Active → Closed`

Also support:

- Paused.
- Cancelled.
- Expired.

These states should be modeled with explicit transition rules rather than arbitrary status updates.

Suggested transition rules:

| Current state | Action | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Draft | Send quotation | Quotation |
| Quotation | Confirm accepted terms | Confirmed |
| Confirmed | Activate subscription | Active |
| Active | Pause, when permitted | Paused |
| Paused | Resume | Active |
| Active | Close under applicable policy | Closed |
| Active | Reach configured expiry | Expired or Closed |
| Active | Cancel, when permitted | Cancelled |

Implement the precise business transitions consistently, including any necessary intermediate confirmation.

For example, a subscription may become active immediately upon confirmation if the business policy permits it. Otherwise, activation can depend on its start date or an explicit activation action.

