# 12. DISCOUNT MANAGEMENT

Only administrators may create or modify discount rules.

## 12.1 Discount configuration

Each discount should include:

- Discount name.
- Unique discount code, if applicable.
- Description.
- Discount type.
- Fixed amount or percentage.
- Minimum purchase amount.
- Minimum quantity.
- Applicable products.
- Applicable plans.
- Whether it applies to individual product lines or an entire subscription.
- Start date.
- End date.
- Maximum total uses.
- Per-customer usage limit, if configured.
- Current usage count.
- Active status.

Support:

- Fixed-amount discounts.
- Percentage discounts.

## 12.2 Discount eligibility

A discount can be applied only when:

- It is active.
- The current billing date is within its validity period.
- The minimum purchase amount is satisfied.
- The minimum quantity is satisfied.
- The applicable product or subscription matches.
- The usage limit has not been reached.
- The customer has not exceeded any configured usage limit.

## 12.3 Recurring discounts

Support recurring discounts that automatically apply to eligible future invoices.

For example:

A customer receives a 10% discount for eligible subscriptions during a defined promotional period.

The discount should:

- Apply automatically to eligible invoices.
- Stop after its expiry date.
- Stop when its usage limit is exhausted.
- Preserve the original discount details on existing invoices.
- Never exceed the permitted discount amount.
- Avoid being counted twice when billing jobs retry.

Track discount usage through durable database records.

When a discount has a limited number of uses, enforce the limit atomically so concurrent billing jobs cannot exceed it.

For percentage discounts, calculate the discount using the applicable line or subscription subtotal according to the configured policy.

For fixed discounts, prevent the discount from reducing the eligible amount below zero.

Display discounts separately on quotations, subscriptions, and invoices.

